    "problem_statement": "The SRP server has no way to be started in a 'fast start' mode: when a device (e.g. a mobile device acting as a provisional border router) joins a Thread network, its SRP server cannot be enabled immediately upon attachment based on whether other border routers are already advertising SRP/DNS services in Network Data. There is no API to enable this mode, no way to query whether it is enabled, and no behavior to start the SRP server quickly on attach when no other SRP/DNS entry exists in Network Data, nor to disable it when another SRP/DNS entry appears.",
